    "answer": "salty-taste/saltiness",
    "mnemonic": "The <kanji>taste</kanji> of <kanji>salt</kanji> is a <vocabulary>salty taste</vocabulary> (it's also when something <vocabulary>tastes salty</vocabulary>).",
    "readingMnemonic": "The readings are the kun'yomi vocab readings. So, take the readings of <ja>塩</ja> (you learned the reading with the kanji) and <ja>味</ja> and you have yourself <ja><reading>しおあじ</reading></ja>.\n\nIf you happen to be a cooking show fan, you might also hear the on'yomi reading of this word - <ja><reading>えんみ</reading></ja>. This word can also be read as <ja><reading>しおみ</reading></ja>, which has more or less the same meaning as the primary reading you learned. ",
